{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1454704-user-could-not-think-of-a-name-for-thread-that-did-not-come-off-as-a-double-entendre","id":1454704,"title":"User Could Not Think of a Name for Thread That Did Not Come Off as a Double-Entendre","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-07-11T12:41:10-07:00","id":1454704,"title":"User Could Not Think of a Name for Thread That Did Not Come Off as a Double-Entendre","content":"Fetishes in Forsaken can make for decent story hooks, whether as rumors, MacGuffins, treasure, or consequences to actions both modern and historical. I thought it might be a useful idea to create a thread where people can post their own fetishes, especially those that are unusual or are more than what they might first appear. Those with particularly interesting histories (whether related to their creation, acquisition, or the spirit bound inside them) are especially appreciated.<br /> <br /> I will start.<br /> <br /> <b>River Fang (5)</b><br /> <br /> This discolored canine is about the length of an adult human finger and is etched in fine, nearly invisible First Tongue runes all along its surface. To access its powers a user must place it in their mouth in the spot where a canine tooth would go (and thus, barring previous accident, must also first get rid of the natural tooth somehow). Once in place and activated, the fetish remains active until it is removed from the user\u2019s mouth.<br /> <br /> The River Fang provides a number of bonuses and alterations to a werewolf who utilizes it. The Uratha\u2019s Dalu, Gauru, Urshul, and Urhan forms become more elongated and slender, with webbing between fingers and paws, granting the ability to swim at full speed and suffering no penalties to Speed or Defense while in water. The Uratha\u2019s Dalu and Gauru forms gain an additional +1 Dexterity. The werewolf\u2019s Urhan form no longer blends in among wolves as it resembles more a wolf-mustelid hybrid (although in exchange the Uratha now calculates Defense using the higher of Wits or Dexterity while in that form), and the tooth\u2019s size stands out in Hishu contrasted with the rest of the user\u2019s mouth, though polite society will tend to gloss its presence as an unfortunate lopsided overbite. In any form, the Uratha can determine if a liquid is polluted or poisoned with a touch (including beverages, though alcohol always registers as a poison), and adds their Size to their Stamina when determining how long they can hold their breath.<br /> <br /> The spirit bound inside this fetish is strange and powerful, with goals of its own related to its ancient history and twisted <i>magath</i> nature. If freed from the Fang, it immediately Fetters itself to the user at no cost, and depending on how it judges its host, it may eventually attempt to Possess or Claim them. Any time the werewolf gains Essence through chewing and devouring, (whether from consuming flesh, hunting spirits, or other buccal acts), roll Primal Urge against five dice. If the spirit wins, the Uratha gains one Essence less from the meal, which is transferred to the fetish instead. How much Essence the spirit requires to escape its prison is left up to the Storyteller, though by now it\u2019s probably getting pretty close.<br /> <br /> Curiously, humans and Wolf-Blooded can also use this fetish. They gain one of the four other forms at random, which they can turn into with an instant action and point of Willpower. This transformation does not inflict Lunacy, and any form ability that costs Essence can instead be used once per scene for free. Instead of <i>Kuruth</i>, the Rage trait of Gauru inflicts the Berserk Condition if the mortal fails the Resolve + Composure roll. They are treated as having Primal Urge 1 for any form trait that calls for it, but not for any other purpose (such as supernatural tolerance or regeneration). A mortal inserting the fetish into their mouth suffers a Breaking Point (and a point of lethal damage if they had to remove a tooth to do so), and the Fang automatically receives a point of Essence whenever the user consumes human, wolf, or werewolf flesh. While benefiting from the fetish, a non-werewolf also gains a Bane of copper.<br /> <br /> The origins of the Fang are an ancient mystery. The fetish was unearthed in an archaeological dig at the Cahokia Mounds, its nature recognized by a Wolf-Blooded research assistant and promptly spirited away to the claws of Bone Shadows for further investigation. Uratha among the Peoria believe that the Fang was most likely consecrated by one of their ancestors. Occultists and shamans wise of such things believe it to be a cast-off fragment of a Pangaean. If this is indeed the case, it is possible the fetish possesses other powers not yet realized or long forgotten.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}